<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Assoc storage survey - June 13. [CORRECTED 14:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Assoc storage survey - June 13. [CORRECTED 14:10 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf) for the week ended June 13:</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 06/13/97  06/06/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     50.31     41.77     21.6	18.0	19.2</p>
<p>West	    103.82     94.36     40.1	36.4	43.9</p>
<p>Total Canada  154.13    136.14     31.4	27.7	32.7</p>
<p>(Corrects figures under &quot;Pct Full&quot; column.)</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 06/13/97: 232.55 bcf, 06/06/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 06/13/97: 259.11 bcf, 06/06/97: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>   ((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
